{"title":"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A rectangle with a diagonal of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is twice as long as it is wide. What is the area of the rectangle? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/3/21391cf6a72886f3082a6210993c291cbf959b56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{1}{4}x^2\\qquad \\textbf{(B) } \\frac{2}{5}x^2\\qquad \\textbf{(C) } \\frac{1}{2}x^2\\qquad \\textbf{(D) } x^2\\qquad \\textbf{(E) } \\frac{3}{2}x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"451\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's set the length to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the width to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so the rectangle has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/8/398d4e966f6a122faf9df59ee04e22aaf6d3c858.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot 1 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> and diagonal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/2/642091f9d6091014be3f8be8bebd95e01bf985a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\sqrt{1^2+2^2} = \\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"155\" height=\"21\" /> (by Pythagoras' theorem).\n</p><p>Now we can plug this value into the answer choices and test which one will give our desired area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. (Note that all of the answer choices contain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" />, so keep in mind that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/0/ee03340874e12687e23774c12bbe9b294446625c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\sqrt{5}\\right)^2 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"88\" height=\"37\" />.)\n</p><p>We eventually find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/f/d0faf780ad6ec5102f2975ab68d49d19922614cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{5} \\cdot \\left(\\sqrt{5}\\right)^2 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"114\" height=\"38\" />, so the correct answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/a/cea8c90e8745128bc763e832d161bce998206d31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } \\frac{2}{5}x^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"79\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>-JinhoK\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Call the length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/4/1a40f8faeab3899443c5ea0672d4899be44aa7ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2l$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> and the width <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" />, so the area of the rectangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/4/ea4af4d109efabc270949aa9efa72a307bf5a1cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2l \\cdot l = 2l^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"82\" height=\"17\" />. As in Solution 1, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is the hypotenuse of the right triangle with legs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/4/1a40f8faeab3899443c5ea0672d4899be44aa7ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2l$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" />, so by Pythagoras' theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/c/49c2425552de042dd4405447f087f03e5362f32c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\sqrt{\\left(2l\\right)^2+l^2} = \\sqrt{4l^2+l^2} = \\sqrt{5l^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -9px\" width=\"285\" height=\"34\" />. This becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/8/ea817060b0c5544d08d53b49001e6d9733dcf239.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l^2 = \\frac{x^2}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"57\" height=\"39\" />, and therefore the area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/4/c84e2a3d59213f796c8492e99274046648f04253.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2l^2 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } \\frac{2}{5}x^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"125\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>-mobius247\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1\">Video Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/X8QyT5RR-_M\">https://youtu.be/X8QyT5RR-_M</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/5Bz7PC-tgyU\">https://youtu.be/5Bz7PC-tgyU</a>\n</p><p>~Charles3829\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A\">2005 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2005 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017204432\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.036 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.056 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 204/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2320/2097152